WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.342
The takeaway is that spherical CNNs were never
fundamentally limited,

00:00:04.422 --> 00:00:06.201
they were just poorly scaled.

00:00:06.281 --> 00:00:10.752
With a redesign of the nonlinearity, normalization,
and residual block,

00:00:10.832 --> 00:00:14.084
plus an implementation tuned to modern accelerators,

00:00:14.164 --> 00:00:16.904
these models finally scale to real problems,

00:00:16.984 --> 00:00:24.339
reaching state of the art on molecular property
prediction and becoming genuinely competitive neural weather models.

00:00:24.419 --> 00:00:30.620
The authors release their JAX implementation as a
platform for further research on spherical data.
